Only the Android dependency closure used by this application is included.
Shared commonMain sources are required by Android; other platform source sets are not included.
SOURCE_MANIFEST.json records hashes for all 205 retained Kotlin files: 150 exact upstream
files and 55 derived subsets. The derived files omit unused declarations/imports or icon
weights; retained declaration bodies and icon path data are unchanged. Default aliases
and Regular icon glyphs are included. No component rendering or animation is rewritten.
231 Android baseline profile rules retain only classes present in the compiled application.

Android build adapters and integration wrappers are provided by ReaMicro Extend.
GlassDialog, GlassDialogButton, GlassCard, GlassTopAppBar, GlassNavigationBar,
GlassIconButton, GlassIconDropdownMenu, GlassDropdownPreference and GlassTextField
use upstream renderers. Glass components retain their upstream opaque fallback.
WindowDialogHost supplies upstream WindowComponentHost; GlassDialog/OverlayDialog
own their contents, scrim and motion. The optional AOSP transition uses the upstream
glassDialogSurface with the application's navigation transition.
WindowPopupScope isolates a platform window's popup roots. Menus render outside the
recorded dialog body, so each glass surface samples only content below it.
The entry-based dropdown adapter follows rc01's value-anchor tracking, fresh-bound
wait and disposal lifecycle while supporting disabled unknown selections.
ScaffoldGlassIconMenu only hosts the menu and follows the upstream anchor lifecycle;
it does not copy popup animation or rendering.
CapturedBackdrop preserves single recording and visibility with rc01's recorder lifecycle.

